    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0088" n="74" xml:id="pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Stettinius Mission/99a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-16T19:00:00-04:00">May 16, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>662. In interviews with Chinese Ambassador Koo<anchor n="55" xml:id="d67-f1"/> in
                    London on April 18 and 25, Under Secretary Stettinius outlined the general
                    course of his discussions with the British.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d67-f2"/> The
                    Under Secretary also told Mr. Koo that an official of the British Foreign Office
                    had stated that the Chinese Embassy would be furnished a written statement in
                    regard to the American-British conversations.</p>
                <p>Ambassador Koo inquired whether the questions of India and of Far Eastern
                    territories (doubtless with Hong Kong in mind) had been discussed with the
                    British; the Under Secretary replied that they had not.</p>
                <p>Dr. Wei had a long interview with the Under Secretary today in which he was
                    informed of the London discussions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d67-f1" n="55" xml:id="d67-f1-content">
                <p>V. K. Wellington Koo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d67-f2" n="56" xml:id="d67-f2-content">
                <p>A statement issued to the press on April 29 jointly by the Under Secretary of
                    State and the British Foreign Secretary indicated that Mr. Stettinius had been
                    visiting in London during the past three weeks for informal and exploratory
                    exchanges of views and that opportunities had been taken to keep the Soviet and
                    Chinese Governments informed as to the course of the discussions.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
